    "media:imagetext": "- 2 -\nwhich hes been under the sane\nfamily managenent for fitteen generations.\nIt is located up an alley in the heart of Kyoto.\nWe took off our shoes\nand climbed some stairs, polished like fine old corcovan by 300 years\nof use plus wax and rubbing.\nSitting cross-legged in the nat covered\nfloor around low tables we ate turtle soup with big hunks of turtle\nmest afloat therein - the speciality of the house. Later - thank\ngoodness not before dinner - they brought in a live snapping turtle\nto show us what we had eaten. It was a good experience to go through -\nonce.\nThe next day, londay, Noverber 10th, we drove over to Nara\nwhere we saw the largest wooden building in the worid - s beautiful\n1,000 year old temple which houses = 60 foot high Buddha.\nWe also ment\nto see a famous big bronze bell, the lergest in Japan, which you cen\nring at the cost of ten yen.\nThe ring is accomplished by a big 1og\nwhich is suspended in such a way as to perrit it being pulled back\nand then swung eg inst the bell.\nThe resulting tone can be heard for\nmiles around.\nDebby financed s delegation oi blind children letting\neach one ring the bell.\nI think her philanthropy come to a total\nof 30¢ but she mede a lot of kids very hapy.\nFrom Nara we crove down to Osake where we had a tenpura\ndinner.\nThis you eat at a counter seated on a stool rather then on\nthe i1oor.\nIt is very good, I'm\ntold.\nNot being able to eat shrimp I sneaked mine along with ny chop-\nsticks to Debby when our hosts weren't looking and made my own dinner\nout of fried eel which was very good but would have been better if I\nhad not known what it was.\nOur trip home from Osaka was uneventiul.\nOur hotel deal is on the track and there is nothing more\nfor me to do here so ve are leaving this evening for Hongkong•\nhe take\noff at 9:00 fly to Okinawa for refueling and then to Hongkong\noverber ith the then say to i it.\nwhere we\nWe stay there until Monday\nDon't know\nas yet just how long we shall stay in the\nPhilippines, but es soon as we do will write again from there.\nI am enclosing the pictures mentioned in the last letter\nwhich as I said are not good but may be of\nsome interest.\nAll the best to sil of you, from\nн. м. В.",
